# PandaCSS Design Token Guide

This guide provides rules and best practices for using design tokens with Panda CSS, ensuring consistent styling across your project

## Desipes and Their Values

### Color Tokens
- **Base tokens**: `colors.blue.600` → Actual value: `#2563eb`
- **Semantic tokens**: `colors.primary` → References base token (e.g., `var(--colors-blue-600)`)
- **Usage**: `bg: 'primary'`, `color: 'primary.foreground'`
- **Opacity modifiers**: Add `/90`, `/10` for opacity variations: `bg: 'primary/90'`

#### Semantic Color Token Naming Convention
Our design system defines the following semantic color tokens in `preset.ts`:

- **background/foreground**: Base page colors
  - `background`: Page background color (white in light mode, slate.950 in dark mode)
  - `foreground`: Text color hierarchy
    - `foreground.DEFAULT`: Primary text color (slate.700 in light mode, slate.300 in dark mode)
    - `foreground.muted`: Secondary text color (slate.500 in light mode, slate.400 in dark mode)
    - `foreground.emphasized`: Strong text color (slate.900 in light mode, slate.100 in dark mode)
    - `foreground.primary`: Brand-aligned text color (blue.600 in light mode, blue.400 in dark mode)
    - `foreground.destructive`: Error text color (red.600 in light mode, red.400 in dark mode)
    - `foreground.inverted`: Inverted text color (white in light mode, slate.950 in dark mode)

- **Layer System**: For managing visual hierarchy
  - `layer.DEFAULT`: Base layer background (white/slate.950)
  - `layer.floating`: Floating element background (slate.50/slate.900)
  - `layer.active`: Active state background (slate.100/slate.800)
  - `layer.overlay`: Overlay background (black/50)

- **Interactive Colors**:
  - `primary`: Main brand color for key actions
    - `primary.DEFAULT`: Primary button background (blue.600/700)
    - `primary.active`: Active state color (blue.700/300)
    - `primary.foreground`: Text on primary buttons (white/slate.50)
  - `secondary`: Supporting color for secondary actions
    - `secondary.DEFAULT`: Secondary button background (gray.700/500)
    - `secondary.active`: Active state color (gray.800/400)
    - `secondary.foreground`: Text on secondary buttons (white/slate.50)
  - `neutral`: Neutral UI elements
    - `neutral.DEFAULT`: Neutral background (slate.100/800)
    - `neutral.active`: Active state color (slate.200/700)
  - `destructive`: Error states and dangerous actions
    - `destructive.DEFAULT`: Delete button, error states (red.600/400)
    - `destructive.active`: Active state color (red.700/300)
    - `destructive.foreground`: Text on destructive elements (white/slate.50)

- **Stroke Colors**:
  - `stroke.DEFAULT`: Default stroke color (slate.300/slate.50)
  - `stroke.subtle`: Subtle borders (slate.200/slate.800)
  - `stroke.interactive`: Interactive element borders (blue.400/blue.500)
  - `stroke.ring`: Focus indicator outlines (blue.500/400)
  - `stroke.destructive`: Destructive element borders (red.500/400)

### Spacing Tokens
- **Number tokens**: `spacing.4` → Actual value: `1rem` (16px)
- **Usage**: `p: '4'`, `gap: '2'`, `px: '4'`, `py: '2'`

### Size Tokens
- **Component sizes**: `sizes.10` → Actual value: `2.5rem` (40px)
- **Usage**: `width: '10'`, `height: '9'`, `w: 'full'`

### Border Tokens
- **Semantic borders**: `borders.base` → Actual value: `1px solid var(--colors-stroke)`
- **Usage**: `border: 'base'`, `border: 'input'`, `border: 'primary'`, `border: 'destructive'`

### Border Radius Tokens
- **Size-based**: `radii.md` → Actual value: `0.375rem` (6px)
- **Usage**: `borderRadius: 'md'`

### Text Style Tokens
- **Size**: `fontSizes.sm` → Actual value: `0.875rem`
- **Weight**: `fontWeights.medium` → Actual value: `500`
- **Usage**: `fontSize: 'sm'`, `fontWeight: 'medium'`
- **Composite styles**: `textStyle: 'body1'` → combines font size, line height, etc.

#### Text Style Categories from preset.ts
Our design system defines the following text styles in `preset.ts`:

- **Display**: Largest text styles for hero sections
  - `display1`: 4.5rem (72px), bold
  - `display2`: 3.75rem (60px), bold

- **Title**: Large text for section headings
  - `title1`: 2.25rem (36px), semibold
  - `title2`: 1.5rem (24px), semibold
  - `title3`: 1.25rem (20px), bold

- **Heading**: Medium text for sub-headings
  - `heading1`: 1.125rem (18px), semibold
  - `heading2`: 1rem (16px), semibold

- **Body**: Standard text for content
  - `body1`: 1rem (16px), normal weight
  - `body2`: 0.875rem (14px), normal weight

- **Label/Caption**: Small text for UI elements
  - `label1`: 0.875rem (14px), semibold
  - `label2`: 0.75rem (12px), semibold
  - `caption1`: 0.75rem (12px), semibold
  - `caption2`: 0.625rem (10px), semibold

## Rules for Token Usage

1. **Always use tokens instead of hardcoded values**
   - ✅ `px: '4'`, `borderRadius: 'md'`, `color: 'primary'`
   - ❌ `padding: '16px'`, `borderRadius: '6px'`, `color: '#2563eb'`

2. **Use semantic tokens when available**
   - ✅ `bg: 'primary'`, `color: 'destructive'`
   - ❌ `bg: 'blue.600'` (when representing a primary action)

3. **For state variations, use condition modifiers first**
   - ✅ `_hover: { bg: 'primary/90' }`
   - ✅ `_disabled: { opacity: '0.5', cursor: 'not-allowed' }`
   - ❌ add hover variant 

4. **Structure recipes (cva/sva) properly**
   - Put common styles in `base`
   - Use `variants` for varying styles
   - Define reasonable `defaultVariants`

5. **Text Color Usage**
   - For page background, use `foreground` variants:
     - `foreground.DEFAULT`: Standard text
     - `foreground.muted`: Secondary text
     - `foreground.emphasized`: Strong text
     - `foreground.primary`: Brand-colored text
     - `foreground.destructive`: Error text
   - For colored backgrounds, use their corresponding foreground colors:
     - Use `primary.foreground` on `primary` background
     - Use `secondary.foreground` on `secondary` background
     - Use `destructive.foreground` on `destructive` background

6. **Text Color Guidelines by Background Context**
   - **Regular background**: Use `foreground` variants on page `background`
     - `foreground.DEFAULT`: Standard text
     - `foreground.muted`: Secondary or less important text
     - `foreground.emphasized`: Strong, important text
     - `foreground.primary`: Brand-aligned text for emphasis or links
     - `foreground.destructive`: Error or warning text
   - **Transparent background**:
     - Use `foreground` variants when parent has the page background
     - Use the corresponding `.foreground` when parent has a specific color background (primary, secondary, etc.)
   - **Text colors for state changes**:
     - Active state: Use appropriate `.foreground` with the color's `.active` background
     - Hover/focus: Use opacity variations (e.g., `primary/90`)
   **Example Code**:
   ```tsx
   // Basic text
   <Text color="foreground">Basic text</Text>
   <Text color="foreground.muted">Secondary text</Text>
   <Text color="foreground.emphasized">Strong text</Text>

   // Important text (on default background)
   <Text color="foreground.primary">Brand text</Text>

   // Button text (on primary background)
   <Button bg="primary" color="primary.foreground">Button text</Button>

   // Warning text
   <Text color="foreground.destructive">Warning text</Text>

   // Layer text (e.g., cards, panels)
   <Card bg="layer.DEFAULT">
     <Text color="foreground.emphasized">Card title</Text>
     <Text color="foreground.muted">Card description</Text>
     <Link color="foreground.primary">Learn more</Link>
   </Card>

   // Text on transparent background (parent has primary background)
   <Box bg="transparent" color="primary.foreground">Text</Box>
   ```

## Example Correct Implementation

```typescript
// Button component recipe with proper token usage
export const buttonRecipe = cva({
  base: {
    display: 'inline-flex',
    alignItems: 'center',
    justifyContent: 'center',
    borderRadius: 'md',
    bg: 'primary',
    color: 'primary.foreground',
    
    _focus: {
      outline: 'none',
      borderColor: 'stroke.ring',
    },
    _disabled: {
      opacity: '0.5',
      cursor: 'not-allowed',
      bg: 'neutral',
      color: 'neutral.foreground',
    }
  },
  variants: {
    size: {
      sm: { height: '9', px: '3', fontSize: 'sm' },
      md: { height: '10', px: '4', fontSize: 'md' },
      lg: { height: '11', px: '8', fontSize: 'lg' }
    },
    variant: {
      outline: {
        bg: 'transparent',
        border: 'input',
        color: 'foreground.emphasized',
        _hover: { bg: 'neutral', color: 'foreground' }
      },
      destructive: {
        bg: 'destructive',
        color: 'destructive.foreground',
        _hover: { bg: 'destructive/90' }
      }
    }
  },
  defaultVariants: {
    size: 'md',
    variant: 'primary'
  }
});
```